questions.question:
POST /auth/login is limited to 5 attempts per 60 s per IP with a fixed window:

const n = await redis.incr(`rl:login:${ip}`);
if (n === 1) await redis.expire(`rl:login:${ip}`, 60);
if (n > 5) throw new TooManyRequestsException();

Access log for one IP (the first attempt of the window was at 10:00:00.000):
10:00:00.000 POST /auth/login 401
10:00:59.600 POST /auth/login 401   (x4, 100 ms apart)
10:01:00.050 POST /auth/login 401   (x5, 100 ms apart)
10:01:00.470 POST /auth/login 429

Statement: "The limiter has a bug: a correct 5-per-60-seconds fixed window would have answered 429 to the five attempts that started at 10:01:00.050."

A different service limits password-reset e-mails per user, 5 per 60 s:

const n = await redis.incr(`rl:reset:${userId}`);
await redis.expire(`rl:reset:${userId}`, 60);     // keep the window fresh
if (n > 5) throw new TooManyRequestsException();

A mobile client retries a failed request automatically every 20 seconds, forever.

Statement: "For this user the key never expires, so from the sixth request on every request is denied, even though the client never sends more than 3 requests in any 60 seconds."
